SUMMARY OF FINDING

Items 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8 and ruling 2026-08-16e all pass. Item 4 FAILS.

The merged tree fixes the three lookups named in the report, but a FOURTH
site of exactly the same class survives, one line below a line A1 did fix,
inside a manifest file:

  internal/services/dataloader/loader.go:1075
      if pair.Left.Hash == decision.SuppressedHash {

`decision.SuppressedHash` is rekeyed to a StableID by A1 (duplicate_
decisions.go:107-108 canonicalKey on save, plus writeDecisionsLocked:156-171
on every write). `pair.Left.Hash` is a legacy content hash. After A1, that
comparison can never be true, so the swap that makes `Left = kept` in the
resolved-pairs list never fires. The immediately preceding line WAS updated
(loader.go:1069, `idxByHash` -> `idxByIdentity`); this one was not.

Consequence: /duplicates renders `.Left` under "Kept" and `.Right` under
"Suppressed" (web/templates/pages/duplicates.html:70-77), and the MCP
list_duplicates tool returns the same pairs (mcpsvc/admin/duplicates.go:110,
119). Whenever the user suppresses the earlier-in-file row, both surfaces now
name the suppressed row as the one that was kept. No error, no log line.

