ITEM 4 - HASH-INDEXED SIDECAR LOOKUPS: FAIL
--------------------------------------------------------------------
(a) The three named sites ARE fixed. Verified by reading the merged code:

  internal/services/insights/trends.go:36-42
      // Pin wins. StableID first, legacy content hash second.
      if id, _, ok := models.ResolveByIdentity(pins, t); ok {
  internal/services/majorexpenses/engine.go:79
      if id, _, ok := models.ResolveByIdentity(opts.Pins, t); ok && validIDs[id] {
  internal/services/majorexpenses/engine.go:128 (AnnotateRecurringPayments)
      if id, _, ok := models.ResolveByIdentity(pins, first); ok && validIDs[id] {

  A fourth pins consumer the report did not name is also fixed:
  internal/services/dataloader/major_expense_names.go:62.

(b) Repo-wide sweep. `git grep -nE '\[[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]*\.Hash\]'` and
`git grep -n '\.Hash\]'` over all *.go returned 24 non-test hits. I triaged
every one. All but two are in-memory maps built from `t.Hash` in the same
pass and read back with `t.Hash` -- self-consistent, never loaded from a
sidecar, so a rekey cannot desynchronize them:
  majorexpenses/engine.go:83 + :253 (PinnedHashes, built at :83, read at
    :253 within the same Match call; deliberately documented at :81-82)
  handlers/majorexpenses/handlers.go:377,378,430 (consume that same
    PinnedHashes from the Match result)
  mcpsvc/curate/expenses.go:93, register.go:129,135,230 (same, plus
    outflowHashSet built at register.go:120-138)
  handlers/explorer/handlers.go:81 (hashToExpense, built from match.Groups)
  amazon/matcher.go:164, anomalies/anomalies.go:193-194,
    mcpsvc/curate/pins.go:75,91, dataloader/loader.go:747-748 (local
    dedup/seen sets)
  models/transaction.go:131 (the fallback arm of ResolveByIdentity itself)
  dataloader/stable_id.go:60-61, loader.go:1035 (index construction)

The two exceptions:
  - dataloader/loader.go:951 `aliases[transactions[i].Hash]` reads the
    aliases.json sidecar by Hash, and SaveAlias (loader.go:931) writes it by
    Hash. Nothing calls rekeyToStable on it (only three call sites exist:
    amazon_enrichment.go:62, duplicate_decisions.go:155,
    transaction_pins.go:65). So aliases stay Hash-keyed on BOTH ends and are
    not broken by A1. NOT a defect -- reported as a residual gap: the alias
    DisplayName is a stored user decision and is still orphaned by a
    description reformat, the very problem A1 exists to solve. Out of A1's
    stated scope (the brief and GLOSSARY name pins, duplicate_decisions,
    amazon_enrichment, and the future transfer_decisions).
  - loader.go:1075 -- the defect. See below.

