(d) PROOF the loader.go:1075 comparison is a live regression. I copied the
repo to a scratch directory OUTSIDE the tree
(/tmp/claude-1000/.../scratchpad/b2copy) and added two probes there. The
repository itself was never modified.

Probe 1 -- end to end through the PUBLIC write path the /duplicates form
actually uses (it posts Transaction.Hash for both sides; see
handlers/duplicates/handlers.go:88-99):

  $ go test -count=1 -v -run TestZZCheck_ResolvedRolesEndToEnd \
      ./internal/services/dataloader/
  === RUN   TestZZCheck_ResolvedRolesEndToEnd
      pair.Left="Lucid" pair.Right="Check #996583"
      stored[05a0d5570576ecfd] kept="usaa-checking|2026-03-20|-158043|0" \
                          suppressed="usaa-checking|2026-03-19|-158043|0"
      PAGE RENDERS -> Kept: "Lucid" | Suppressed: "Check #996583"
      duplicates page shows "Lucid" under "Kept", but the user kept "Check #996583"
  --- FAIL: TestZZCheck_ResolvedRolesEndToEnd (0.00s)

  The user kept the check and suppressed "Lucid". SaveDuplicateDecision
  correctly rewrote both identities to StableIDs (see the `stored[...]` line).
  The next load stamped Suppressed on the right row -- that assertion did NOT
  fire, so aggregates and Active() are correct. But ResolvedDuplicates()
  returned Left="Lucid", i.e. the page labels the SUPPRESSED row as "Kept".

Probe 2 -- the same scenario in the pre-StableID legacy form, as a control:

  === RUN   TestZZCheck_ResolvedRolesAfterRekey     (modern stored form)
      resolved[0].Left = "Lucid", want the KEPT row "Check #996583"
  --- FAIL: TestZZCheck_ResolvedRolesAfterRekey
  === RUN   TestZZCheck_ResolvedRolesLegacyForm     (pre-A1 stored form)
      legacy resolved[0].Left  = "Check #996583"
      legacy resolved[0].Right = "Lucid"
  --- PASS: TestZZCheck_ResolvedRolesLegacyForm

  The legacy form gets the roles right and the rekeyed form does not. That
  is what makes this a REGRESSION INTRODUCED BY A1 rather than a
  pre-existing defect: before A1, SuppressedHash was always a content hash
  and the comparison worked.

Blast radius of the defect:
  - web/templates/pages/duplicates.html:70-77 -- the "Suppressed" section
    prints `.Left` under "Kept" and `.Right` under "Suppressed".
  - internal/handlers/duplicates/handlers.go:73 feeds it.
  - internal/services/mcpsvc/admin/duplicates.go:110,119 -- list_duplicates
    with include_resolved returns the same inverted pairs to the LLM.
  Data correctness (Suppressed stamping, totals, Undo by pair key) is
  unaffected. This is a labeling inversion, and it is silent.

Related, lower-severity: mcpsvc/admin/resolve.go:162 echoes
`decision.SuppressedHash` back to the caller, which is now a StableID, while
the tool's own jsonschema at resolve.go:20 documents that field as "the hash
of the side to EXCLUDE, from list_duplicates". The contract text and the
value no longer agree. Not the reason for this FAIL.

