--------------------------------------------------------------------
ITEM 6 - REKEY ON SAVE, ORPHANS PRESERVED: PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------
rekeyToStable (stable_id.go:143-161) skips a key the index does not resolve
(`if !ok || stable == key { continue }`) -- it only ever moves a key it can
identify, and never deletes an unresolvable one. Called from exactly three
save paths: transaction_pins.go:65 (writePinsLocked),
duplicate_decisions.go:155, amazon_enrichment.go:62.
WriteTransactionPins (transaction_pins.go:74-81) correctly does NOT rekey --
it routes to writePinsRawLocked, satisfying the pinned-API requirement that
it persist verbatim.

Covered by TestSetTransactionPin_RekeysResolvedEntriesAndKeepsOrphans
(stable_id_test.go:246-296), which asserts a 3-entry count first, then that
the resolved legacy key moved to vet.StableID, that the old key is gone,
and that `pins[orphan] == "me-vet"` -- the unresolvable key is preserved,
not dropped. It also asserts unpin-by-legacy-hash still reaches the rekeyed
entry (canonicalKey, stable_id.go:120-128). Passes in the merged tree.

