(only a trailing blank line from my sed range; the function body is byte
identical -- it still keys on `seen[t.Hash]` at loader.go:747-748)

$ git grep -n 'StableID' -- '*.go' | grep -v _test
No hit inside ComputeHash, deduplicateTransactions, or classifier. StableID
does not participate in dedup anywhere.

Both directions are asserted by
TestDeduplicateTransactions_IgnoresStableID (stable_id_test.go:432-453):
same Hash + StableIDs "a|...|0" vs "b|...|7" -> 1 row; Hashes h1/h2 +
identical StableID "a|2026-01-01|-2000|0" -> 2 rows. Plus
TestLoadData_DedupUnchangedAcrossOverlappingExports (:458) at the load level,
which also pins the survivor to the first file-order occurrence. Both pass.

Note: assignStableIDs runs BEFORE dedup (loader.go:345, ahead of
filterInternalTransfers/classify/dedup), matching GLOSSARY's pipeline step 4
and keeping the occurrence index counted over everything parsed. Its
first-occurrence-wins index (stable_id.go:59-63) is correct: dedup keeps the
first row, so pointing a legacy hash at the second row's StableID would
rekey a pin onto a row about to disappear.

