ITEM 8 - SCOPE AND THE CHANGED PRE-EXISTING TEST: PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope is clean. The 13 manifest files contain no transfer classification (no
internal/services/transfers package; loader.go still calls the old
filterInternalTransfers at line 348), no balance work beyond A4's, no
web/ or template changes, and no MCP tool additions (nothing under
internal/services/mcpsvc/ is touched).

The coverage_test.go change is LEGITIMATE, not papering over a regression.
The test pins via `dl.SetTransactionPin(hash, ...)` (coverage_test.go:620),
which canonicalizes the posted legacy hash to the row's StableID
(transaction_pins.go:115-119). So `pins[hash]` is legitimately absent
afterwards -- that is behavior 3 working, exactly what the old assertion
encoded against. The replacement `if id, ok := dl.PinFor(ts.Transactions[0]);
!ok || id == ""` is no weaker: it still fails if the pin was not stored, and
it now goes through the documented read path. It also keeps the original
diagnostic (dumping the pins map on failure) and does not change what the
test covers (`match.PinnedHashes[t.Hash]` in the summary loop, which still
works because PinnedHashes is Hash-keyed by construction at engine.go:83).

